## The correction of `L-0000004`, recorded here because it may not be recorded there

`L-0000004`'s **prose body was produced by incrementing the identifiers in `L-0000003`'s and
was never rewritten.** It therefore describes the *second* round's canonical-path defect,
cites 846 tests and mutations M8–M13, states that `S-2026-08-17-01` wrote `L-0000003`, and
says the work waits on a *third* cold round. Every one of those sentences is about the wrong
session.

**What is true of `L-0000004`:** all seven DC-3-covered fields — `seq`, `timestamp`,
`session_id`, `actor`, `action`, `artifacts`, `prev_hash` — are correct; its `action` describes
`S-2026-08-17-03` accurately; its digest recomputes; the chain links; `HEAD` reconciles.
**No digest moves and the tamper-evidence is intact.** The falsehood is confined to prose that
DC-3 does not cover, which is the exposure `OI-C-01` records in the general case.

**Why it stands.** The artifact is `append-only`. Rewriting an entry's account so a session
reads better is the precise act this chain exists to make detectable, and doing it here — in
the ledger, to tidy a record of my own work — would be worse than the error. **A false account
left standing and annotated is a smaller failure than a corrected one that leaves no trace.**
Found by the fourth independent round as its FIND-5.

## What this entry records

**The fourth round found that the check written to end a recurring defect did not catch that
defect**, while four artifacts claimed it did. Its pattern was line-scoped and the defect's own
phrasing spans lines; **2 of 9 sequence phrasings and 2 of 9 head phrasings were caught**, and
its self-test was circular — validating the pattern against a string written for the pattern.

Rebuilt as `python -m aief_register` with a rule that is structural rather than lexical:
**outside a blockquote, in a section that governs, an identifier must be the live one.** The
first attempt at *that* was also wrong — a keyword window over prose flagged **thirty**
assertions, almost all of them a register *recounting* the defect — and the reason is recorded
at the module: **a rule that cannot tell "X is current" from "X was wrongly called current" is
a trap for the honest.** 21 tests now replay every phrasing the round found evading, and two
assert the converse.

`ECR-D-014` is **not** closed. Its substance has been re-proved cold twice and round 3
declared its enforcement condition fully discharged; what holds it is record accuracy, and
LAW-05 bars this session from certifying its own corrections. Fourth time.

**No new open item was raised, and `OI-C-10` is why** — the index stands at 597 of 600 against
a marginal cost of ~5. **That is the second finding in two sessions that could not be given an
identifier**, and it is the clearest available statement of what `OI-C-10` now costs.

